recommendation:
1. Build E2's evaluation layer now, whatever is decided about E2's learning. That is a matrix unit with:
   - item-blocked interleaved dispatch;
   - r = 2 runs;
   - per-cell request hashing;
   - a byte-identical duplicate canary and a length-matched placebo;
   - regime logging;
   - no reuse across sessions.
   Cross-session comparisons are invalid everywhere in the project (drift of up to 24 points), so this repairs every comparison, not only E2's.
2. Run D0 first: about 48-95M deepseek tokens and no learning. Re-evaluate the existing v1 SearchQA-learned Skills (E-glm s1, GEPA s1, SkillOpt s1) as-is and on top of the cards, together with N, I5, I5b and the placebo, in one interleaved round on OfficeQA, LiveMath and SpreadsheetBench, test + train.
   - This gives the first properly controlled single-source row for our method and both baselines.
   - It also settles whether the GLM-era +19 OfficeQA format effect exists with deepseek. The pilot suggests it may not.
3. Launch learning chains only after D1 makes learning accept rules.
   - Start with design D (264M) or A (381M), with the registered primary "matrix-mean G_all versus the cards".
   - Use R of 2 or more chains per source, K = 3 fresh-batch steps, a General section, source-only regression panels, and r = 2 on test + train panels.
   - Report every cell versus the cards, versus no Skill and versus the placebo.
4. Owner decisions:
   - (a) whether target training pools may be off-diagonal evaluation panels (more power) or only the test splits (purity);
   - (b) the source set (QA core first);
   - (c) whether a well-measured null matrix ("single-source evolution transfers format, not knowledge") is an acceptable paper result.
5. Do not present the v1 Q1 +2.6 / Q2 +4.1 / Q3 -0.6 or any versus-no-Skill off-diagonal gain as learned generalisation.
